{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0EVX", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-mayer-vietoris}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d446c3723a602cfffd843fc1b576b5ed3597ac0df06aa121db792f0ac31ae1db", "source_text": "Mayer-Vietoris", "source_text_hash": "sha256:32131d10ed001fdcec2500e76b161d4ff74ccd476298431bccf7a397b280f876", "unit_id": "tag:0EVX:title"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0EVX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nE \\ar[d] \\ar[r] & Y \\ar[d] \\\\\nZ \\ar[r] & X\n}\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$K$", "MATH_0005": "$D(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nR\\Gamma(X, K) \\to\nR\\Gamma(Z, K) \\oplus\nR\\Gamma(Y, K) \\to\nR\\Gamma(E, K)\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{cohomology-section-mayer-vietoris}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f55008bca20a2eff920be7a9fc4c4aeb48ad87e8fc147f0045940595d9032721", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b287f57430eb20e434f0fb4f0fa707011328ff374950a331ba43051defe80523", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nFor the usual statement and proof of Mayer-Vietoris, please\nsee Cohomology, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a ringed site. Consider a\ncommutative diagram\n<MATH_0002>\nin the category <MATH_0003>. In this situation, given an object\n<MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005> we get what looks like the\nbeginning of a distinguished triangle\n<MATH_0006>\nIn the following lemma we make this more precise.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:916cee867183a7f071be11fdcad03b44b09b406b98358ebe5f88d53ffb037621", "unit_id": "tag:0EVX:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0EVX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0003": "$K$", "MATH_0004": "$-1$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet(X) \\xrightarrow{\\alpha}\n\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet(Z) \\oplus\n\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet(Y) \\xrightarrow{\\beta}\n\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet(E)\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$\\beta \\circ \\alpha = 0$", "MATH_0007": "$$\nc^K_{X, Z, Y, E} :\n\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet(X)\n\\longrightarrow\nC(\\beta)^\\bullet[-1]\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$K$", "MATH_0009": "$c^K_{X, Z, Y, E}$", "MATH_0010": "$$\nR\\Gamma(X, K) \\to\nR\\Gamma(Z, K) \\oplus\nR\\Gamma(Y, K) \\to\nR\\Gamma(E, K) \\to\nR\\Gamma(X, K)[1]\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$K$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-c-square}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a6f4514fe3e170220626fc85b0dfb8fae93337b680b50c64b21f882fd8bc56a7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e33fd7f6e34a01a7d63c0c01387f3b945e1169a6c862eb1883272135f3cede66", "source_text": "In the situation above, choose a K-injective complex <MATH_0001>\nof <MATH_0002>-modules representing <MATH_0003>. Using <MATH_0004> times the canonical map\nfor one of the four arrows we get maps of complexes\n<MATH_0005>\nwith <MATH_0006>. Thus a canonical map\n<MATH_0007>\nThis map is canonical in the sense that a different choice\nof K-injective complex representing <MATH_0008> determines an isomorphic\narrow in the derived category of abelian groups. If <MATH_0009>\nis an isomorphism, then using its inverse we obtain a canonical\ndistinguished triangle\n<MATH_0010>\nAll of these constructions are functorial in <MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:38b69d864fbd1e90d7501196bfd71c6d88db863f43a08221845fa946f1610e7b", "unit_id": "tag:0F16:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0EVX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{J}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0002": "$K$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{I}^\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{J}^\\bullet$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{derived-section-cones}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{derived-section-homotopy-triangulated}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:72f57a222723d3cd0df43b0b3b3d59ac7037fa192ff5e40d13e3a37d3276a519", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d95426d54762a5e38b62d43b170ef1b1e032ab7d80a306f620b5b78f66962d53", "source_text": "This lemma proves itself. For example, if <MATH_0001>\nis a second K-injective complex representing <MATH_0002>, then\nwe can choose a quasi-isomorphism\n<MATH_0003>\nwhich determines quasi-isomorphisms between all the complexes\nin sight. Details omitted. For the construction of cones\nand the relationship with distinguished triangles see\nDerived Categories, Sections <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a5731695efcc446a18926df8f59ca85b284a2f852f29e1b1cd13d9394f5470fa", "unit_id": "tag:0F16:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0EVX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$K_1 \\to K_2 \\to K_3 \\to K_1[1]$", "MATH_0002": "$D(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0003": "$c^{K_i}_{X, Z, Y, E}$", "MATH_0004": "$i$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{1, 2, 3\\}$", "MATH_0006": "$i$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-two-out-of-three-blow-up-square}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a2c5dfc92f7521d59d6cfb24e1e20113ee01bfa6512fe771e18a56a302f4df82", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bbcdffe9c39211e60d187fe6ea08220d1729bf37c11f486f8a86fbabe595b321", "source_text": "In the situation above, let <MATH_0001> be a distinguished\ntriangle in <MATH_0002>.\nIf <MATH_0003> is a quasi-isomorphism for\ntwo <MATH_0004> out of <MATH_0005>, then it is a quasi-isomorphism\nfor the third <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:693efbe9330f83aa0b4ab9a8fb4b7666957107765ec9bf835b2bc9286527eacf", "unit_id": "tag:0EWP:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0EVX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$c^{K_1}_{X, Z, Y, E}$", "MATH_0002": "$c^{K_2}_{X, Z, Y, E}$", "MATH_0003": "$f : \\mathcal{I}^\\bullet_1 \\to \\mathcal{I}^\\bullet_2$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0005": "$K_1 \\to K_2$", "MATH_0006": "$K_3$", "MATH_0007": "$C(f)^\\bullet$", "MATH_0008": "$c^{K_3}_{X, Z, Y, E}$", "MATH_0009": "$K(\\textit{Ab})$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{derived-lemma-triangle-K-injective}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{derived-lemma-third-isomorphism-triangle}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:70587bff5cc5baccd8c85f018cff6690b65f2ff25bddebc98abf48af7a7bbae5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:461976e0590c9605738e6d7d340c690eb250e8be7ac448cbad8abdb1b738bb07", "source_text": "By rotating the triangle we may assume <MATH_0001> and\n<MATH_0002> are quasi-isomorphisms. Choose a map\n<MATH_0003> of\nK-injective complexes of <MATH_0004>-modules representing <MATH_0005>.\nThen <MATH_0006> is represented by the K-injective complex\n<MATH_0007>, see\nDerived Categories, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThen the morphism <MATH_0008> is an isomorphism\nas it is the third leg in a map of distinguished triangles\nin <MATH_0009> whose other two legs are quasi-isomorphisms.\nSome details omitted; use\nDerived Categories, Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:71fb4d2731d6e7c3e2ea244ff83843a98311fe83edb284ca2b6a4d7ea68596b9", "unit_id": "tag:0EWP:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0EVX", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:50c99353882e5e5d40c13174d353753a3d6b51ecf31b77199a55e17649a15d39", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet us give a criterion for when this does produce\na distinguished triangle.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8c12ebfebcb329f579bef9baacd52c253c688b80d0fd3ffc15fe55b86c2f3f25", "unit_id": "tag:0EVX:prose-0002"}
